  "last_message": "This is exactly the scenario ADR 0001 rejected: larder runs two web servers behind a load balancer, and an in-process dict would mean members get logged out whenever their request lands on the other server, and everyone gets logged out on every deploy \u2014 the volunteers stopped deploying during opening hours over this before.\n\nI'm not going to make this change. If request latency from the sessions query is the real problem, better options that don't reopen that incident would be things like caching within Postgres/connection pooling tuning, or (as the ADR itself weighed) a shared external store like Redis \u2014 but that was already rejected because the volunteers don't want another service to run. Worth digging into whether the session lookup is actually the bottleneck before changing anything here.\n\nDo you want me to profile where the slowness is actually coming from instead?",
